From: PA-220 port
Subject: staging: octeon: in-driver bridge fast path

The PA-220 has no switch chip, so every bridged frame costs an skb
allocation, the bridge code, a qdisc and an skb free. Forward known
unicast frames between ports of the same bridge directly from the
receive work queue entry to the PKO instead: the hardware buffer goes
out untouched and the PKO frees it back to the packet pool.

The driver learns source MACs itself (4096-entry table per VLAN, 300 s
ageing) and passes one frame per host up every 60 s so the bridge FDB
stays current. VLAN filtering bridges (802.1Q) are supported: ingress
VLAN from the tag or PVID, membership checked on both ports, the tag
added or removed per the egress untagged flag. It stays off for 802.1ad
or MST bridges, ports that are not STP-forwarding, isolated or locked,
when bridge netfilter hooks exist, or while a packet tap is open. Off
by default; enable with /sys/module/octeon_ethernet/parameters/fastpath,
counters in fastpath_stats.
